{
 "description": "Documentaries about one person's life. The arc is a life, told in order: origins, turning points, work, legacy. Personal detail is held to the same evidence discipline as any fact — a life is not improved by inventing it.",
 "entity_handling": [
  "Never invent biographical detail — birthplaces, dates, relationships, motives or private conversations appear only when the script or a retrieved source states them.",
  "Living subjects and their families are treated with care: contested claims about a living person are attributed to their source, never narrated as settled fact.",
  "A subject's own words are quoted only from a retrieved source that carries them; paraphrase is labelled by its framing, never dressed as quotation."
 ],
